{{!-- GOON FACTORY — the rebuilt generator window (GOON-FACTORY-SPEC.md §1).

      Markup only: every string comes from lang/en.json, every rule from css/cp2020-augmented.css
      (.cp-goon-*). The QUICK/FULL split is GONE — there is ONE form whose quick path is
      "Outfit-or-(Role+Grade) → Generate", and every dial below the line is Advanced-gated.

      Each control the JS reads back is selected by its cp-goon-* class (_readForm), so renaming one
      breaks the read. Controls below the line carry `disabled` until Advanced is ticked — §1's
      "locked, visible" state, which is a DISABLED control showing its derived value, never a
      hidden one.

      ⭐ THE FOUR SPEC-DELTA RULINGS OF 2026-08-14, walked on the shipped window, all live here:
        R1 the picks read TOP-DOWN in hierarchy order — threat level, then role, then outfit (the
           outfit still prefills everything below it; only its POSITION moved);
        R2 the Advanced checkbox is ALWAYS live — it was disabled until a grade was picked, which
           reads as a broken control to anyone who clicks it;
        R3 the dial section renders from FIRST OPEN, locked and dashed. The grade-conditional wrap
           that used to hide the whole section contradicted the "locked, visible" rule stated two
           paragraphs up: an underived control shows a DASH, it does not vanish;
        R4 the count remembers the GM's last entry (npcgen-app.js holds the store).

      ⭐ THE FIVE ROUND-2 RULINGS OF 2026-08-14, walked on the repaired window:
        R6 the ticks are MARKS DRAWN ON THE TRACK — BODY at the BTM breakpoints, the stat pool at its
           named tiers, REF tickless by its own ruling. They were <datalist> marks before, which the
           two cores' browsers render differently and one not at all, so the ticks the spec asks for
           were invisible. Each mark carries ONE number, its position; the stylesheet draws it.
        R7 the reservation is a SHADED BAND on the track, from the left edge to the reservation
           point, on the skill-points slider AND the stat-pool slider. The track's total no longer
           moves: the band grows as the threat level rises and the free segment visibly shrinks. The
           slider's `min` used to BE the floor, which is why nothing was drawable; the floor now
           rides as `data-cp-floor` and the window's input handler clamps the thumb onto the band's
           edge. The breakdown line stays and states the same numbers the band draws.
        R8 Luck and Reputation are grouped under a "per-goon rolled stats" mini-section with one
           hint line, because "Luck formula" alone does not say who rolls it or when.
        R9 the armor Weight options name the stat they filter on — armor.js `weightClassOf` splits at
           EV ≤ 1 / EV ≥ 2, so the labels say EV 0–1 and EV 2+ (i18n only; the mechanism is untouched).
        LOOT the dial displays as CARRIED CASH & CONSUMABLES (its key is unchanged), and the preview
           carries a SALVAGE line: the dial cannot gate gear, so the window discloses what the squad
           is worth instead of pretending the dial decides it. --}}
<div class="cp-goon">

  {{#if catalogLoading}}
  {{!-- Awaiting the catalog index in _prepareContext is what would hold the window shut on first
        open, so this panel stands in and the window re-renders when the build lands. --}}
  <p class="cp-goon-pending">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.CatalogLoading"}}</p>
  {{else}}

  {{!-- ── HEADER BAND (R1): threat level · role · outfit · count · Advanced ────────────────── --}}
  <div class="cp-goon-band">
    <div class="cp-goon-row cp-goon-grade-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-grade">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.GradeLabel"}}</label>
      <select id="cp-goon-grade" class="cp-goon-grade">
        {{!-- §1: the threat level initializes to DASHES — an unpicked grade is a real state, not a
              silent default to E. --}}
        <option value="" {{#unless grade}}selected{{/unless}}>{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.GradeUnset"}}</option>
        {{#each grades as |g|}}
        <option value="{{g.key}}" {{#if g.selected}}selected{{/if}} title="{{g.hint}}">{{g.label}}</option>
        {{/each}}
      </select>
    </div>

    {{!-- ROLE. The first option is RANDOM and it is the window's default state (ruled 2026-08-15):
          each goon then rolls its OWN role at generation, so one batch can hold a Cop and a Techie.
          Picking an outfit prefills the outfit's role over that default; flipping back to Random is
          an override like any other and sticks. The option list already leads with Random, so there
          is nothing conditional here. --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row cp-goon-role-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-role" title="{{localize 'CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.RoleHint'}}">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.RoleLabel"}}</label>
      <select id="cp-goon-role" class="cp-goon-role">
        {{#each roles as |r|}}
        <option value="{{r.key}}" {{#if r.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{r.label}}</option>
        {{/each}}
      </select>
    </div>

    {{!-- The outfit is the LAST pick and still the strongest one: picking it prefills the two
          controls above and every dial below. Its "based on" line and its grade-span note travel
          with it.

          The catalogue is RATIFIED (2026-08-14), so the seed suffix and the "three seed outfits
          ship" note are gone: there is nothing provisional left to disclose. What stands in their
          place is §B.2's grade-span note, which renders only for an outfit that HAS a paired
          entry. --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row cp-goon-outfit-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-outfit">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.OutfitLabel"}}</label>
      <select id="cp-goon-outfit" class="cp-goon-outfit">
        <option value="">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.OutfitNone"}}</option>
        {{#each outfits as |o|}}
        <option value="{{o.id}}" {{#if o.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{o.label}}</option>
        {{/each}}
      </select>
    </div>
    {{#if outfitId}}
    <p class="cp-goon-basedon">{{basedOnLabel}}</p>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if gradeSpanNote}}
    <p class="cp-goon-hint cp-goon-spannote">{{gradeSpanNote}}</p>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- DISPOSITION — a BASELINE control (ruled 2026-08-15), which is why it is HERE, inside the
          header band, and not down in `.cp-goon-dials` behind the Advanced checkbox. It carries no
          `disabled` state at all: the Advanced lock starts below this band. An outfit prefills it and
          the GM flips it freely; the value lands on the generated actor's PROTOTYPE TOKEN. --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row cp-goon-disposition-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-disposition" title="{{localize 'CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.DispositionHint'}}">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.DispositionLabel"}}</label>
      <select id="cp-goon-disposition" class="cp-goon-disposition">
        {{#each dispositions as |d|}}
        <option value="{{d.key}}" {{#if d.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{d.label}}</option>
        {{/each}}
      </select>
    </div>

    <div class="cp-goon-row cp-goon-count-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-count">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.CountLabel"}}</label>
      <input id="cp-goon-count" class="cp-goon-count" type="number" min="1" max="{{maxCount}}" value="{{count}}" />
      {{#if countClamped}}<span class="cp-goon-clamp">{{CPLocal "GoonFactory.CountClamped" max=maxCount}}</span>{{/if}}
    </div>

    {{!-- R2: no `disabled` here, under any state. --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row cp-goon-advanced-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-check" for="cp-goon-advanced" title="{{localize 'CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.AdvancedHint'}}">
        <input id="cp-goon-advanced" class="cp-goon-advanced" type="checkbox"
               data-action="goonAdvanced" {{#if advanced}}checked{{/if}} />
        {{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.Advanced"}}
      </label>
    </div>
  </div>

  {{!-- ── BELOW THE LINE (R3): ALWAYS RENDERED. Locked until Advanced; dashed until a grade. ── --}}
  <div class="cp-goon-dials{{#unless advanced}} cp-goon-locked{{/unless}}{{#unless grade}} cp-goon-unset{{/unless}}">
    <p class="cp-goon-section">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.DialsSection"}}</p>
    {{#unless grade}}<p class="cp-goon-hint cp-goon-unset-hint">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.DialsUnsetHint"}}</p>{{/unless}}
    {{#unless advanced}}<p class="cp-goon-hint">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.DialsLockedHint"}}</p>{{/unless}}

    {{!-- REF. `refValue` parks the thumb at the bottom of the range while nothing is derived; the
          READOUT is what tells the truth about that state, and it reads a dash.

          Every slider sits in a `.cp-goon-slider-wrap`, ticked or not, so the four rows keep the
          same height and the tick strip has a box to be positioned in. REF carries no ticks and no
          band — its ruling leaves it plain. --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-ref" title="{{localize 'CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.RefHint'}}">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.RefLabel"}}</label>
      <span class="cp-goon-slider-wrap">
        <input id="cp-goon-ref" class="cp-goon-ref cp-goon-slider" type="range" min="{{refRange.min}}" max="{{refRange.max}}"
               value="{{refValue}}" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}} />
      </span>
      <output class="cp-goon-out">{{refOut}}</output>
    </div>

    {{!-- BT: constant 7 at every grade, with the always-visible stakes line §1 demands.
          R6: the marks are the BTM breakpoints 3/5/8/10. Each carries its position as one number in
          `--cp-tick`; the stylesheet turns that into a mark and the band hover rides the mark's
          own title. --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-bt">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.BtLabel"}}</label>
      <span class="cp-goon-slider-wrap">
        <input id="cp-goon-bt" class="cp-goon-bt cp-goon-slider" type="range" min="{{btRange.min}}" max="{{btRange.max}}"
               value="{{btValue}}" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}} />
        <span class="cp-goon-ticks cp-goon-bt-ticks">
          {{#each btTicks as |t|}}<span class="cp-goon-tick" style="--cp-tick:{{t.pct}}" data-value="{{t.value}}" title="{{t.hint}}"></span>{{/each}}
        </span>
      </span>
      <output class="cp-goon-out">{{btOut}}</output>
    </div>
    <p class="cp-goon-stakes">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.BtStakes"}}</p>

    {{!-- Skill points (R7): the track runs the FULL scale and the grade's weapon-skill guarantee is
          drawn on it as a band from the left edge. `data-cp-floor` is the clamp the band's edge
          represents — the window's input handler holds the thumb there. --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-skillpoints">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.SkillPointsLabel"}}</label>
      <span class="cp-goon-slider-wrap">
        <input id="cp-goon-skillpoints" class="cp-goon-skillpoints cp-goon-slider" type="range"
               min="{{skillScale.scaleMin}}" max="{{skillScale.scaleMax}}" data-cp-floor="{{skill.floor}}"
               value="{{skillValue}}" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}} />
      </span>
      <output class="cp-goon-out">{{skillOut}}</output>
    </div>
    <p class="cp-goon-breakdown" title="{{localize 'CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.SkillReservedHint'}}">{{skillBreakdownLine}}</p>

    {{!-- Stat pool (R6 + R7): named-tier ticks AND a reserved band. The band ends at the dynamic
          floor — REF + BODY, plus the minimum the remaining stats must keep — which is exactly where
          the thumb stops, and exactly what the breakdown line below states in words. --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-statpool">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.StatPoolLabel"}}</label>
      <span class="cp-goon-slider-wrap">
        <input id="cp-goon-statpool" class="cp-goon-statpool cp-goon-slider" type="range"
               min="{{poolScale.scaleMin}}" max="{{poolScale.ceiling}}" data-cp-floor="{{pool.floor}}"
               value="{{poolValue}}" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}} />
        <span class="cp-goon-ticks cp-goon-pool-ticks">
          {{#each poolTicks as |t|}}<span class="cp-goon-tick" style="--cp-tick:{{t.pct}}" data-value="{{t.value}}" title="{{t.hint}}"></span>{{/each}}
        </span>
      </span>
      <output class="cp-goon-out">{{poolOut}}</output>
    </div>
    <p class="cp-goon-breakdown" title="{{localize 'CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.PoolReservedHint'}}">{{poolBreakdownLine}}</p>

    {{!-- Stat shape --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-shape">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.ShapeLabel"}}</label>
      <select id="cp-goon-shape" class="cp-goon-shape" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}}>
        {{#each shapes as |s|}}
        <option value="{{s.key}}" {{#if s.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{s.label}}</option>
        {{/each}}
      </select>
    </div>

    {{!-- R8 — PER-GOON ROLLED STATS. These two are the only dials on the window that are not a
          setting at all: they are dice the generator rolls once per goon, so a GM reading "Luck
          formula" at face value cannot tell whether it is a value, a cap or a roll. The heading and
          the single hint line answer that; the fields, their defaults and their mechanics are
          untouched. --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-rolled">
      <p class="cp-goon-subhead">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.RolledSection"}}</p>
      <p class="cp-goon-hint">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.RolledHint"}}</p>
      <div class="cp-goon-row">
        <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-luck">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.LuckLabel"}}</label>
        <input id="cp-goon-luck" class="cp-goon-luck" type="text" value="{{luckFormula}}" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}} />
      </div>
      <div class="cp-goon-row">
        <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-rep">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.RepLabel"}}</label>
        <input id="cp-goon-rep" class="cp-goon-rep" type="text" value="{{repFormula}}" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}} />
      </div>
      {{#if formulaNote}}<p class="cp-goon-warn">{{formulaNote}}</p>{{/if}}
    </div>

    {{!-- Chromed --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-check" for="cp-goon-chrome-on">
        <input id="cp-goon-chrome-on" class="cp-goon-chrome-on" type="checkbox" {{#if chromeOn}}checked{{/if}} {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}} />
        {{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.ChromedLabel"}}
      </label>
      {{!-- A number input cannot render a dash, so the underived state is an EMPTY field with the
            dash as its placeholder — the same "nothing picked yet" reading. --}}
      <input id="cp-goon-chrome-count" class="cp-goon-chrome-count" type="number" min="0" max="20"
             value="{{chromeCountValue}}" placeholder="{{unsetMark}}" title="{{chromeDerivationLine}}"
             {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}} />
      <span class="cp-goon-hint">{{chromeDerivationLine}}</span>
    </div>

    {{!-- Garnish --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-check" for="cp-goon-garnish">
        <input id="cp-goon-garnish" class="cp-goon-garnish" type="checkbox" {{#if garnish}}checked{{/if}} {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}} />
        {{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.GarnishLabel"}}
      </label>
      <span class="cp-goon-hint">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.GarnishHint"}}</span>
    </div>

    {{!-- Armor filters --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-armor-weight">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.ArmorWeightLabel"}}</label>
      <select id="cp-goon-armor-weight" class="cp-goon-armor-weight" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}}>
        {{#each armorWeights as |w|}}<option value="{{w.key}}" {{#if w.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{w.label}}</option>{{/each}}
      </select>
      <select id="cp-goon-armor-hardness" class="cp-goon-armor-hardness" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}}>
        {{#each armorHardnesses as |h|}}<option value="{{h.key}}" {{#if h.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{h.label}}</option>{{/each}}
      </select>
      <select id="cp-goon-armament" class="cp-goon-armament" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}}>
        {{#each armaments as |a|}}<option value="{{a.key}}" {{#if a.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{a.label}}</option>{{/each}}
      </select>
    </div>
    {{#if armorClampLine}}<p class="cp-goon-warn">{{armorClampLine}}</p>{{/if}}

    {{!-- Loot: OFF by default (GM consent) --}}
    <div class="cp-goon-row">
      <label class="cp-goon-label" for="cp-goon-loot">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.LootLabel"}}</label>
      <select id="cp-goon-loot" class="cp-goon-loot" {{#unless advanced}}disabled{{/unless}}>
        {{#each lootDial as |l|}}<option value="{{l.key}}" {{#if l.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{l.label}}</option>{{/each}}
      </select>
      <span class="cp-goon-hint">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.LootHint"}}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  {{!-- ── PREVIEW: the Generate confirmation step ──────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
  {{#if hasPreview}}
  <div class="cp-goon-preview">
    <p class="cp-goon-section">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.PreviewSection"}}</p>
    {{!-- THE SALVAGE DISCLOSURE. Squad-wide, and printed at every setting of the carried-cash dial:
          gear, armor and chrome are on the goons whatever that dial says, so the window states what
          they are worth rather than leaving the GM to add it up. --}}
    {{#if salvageLine}}<p class="cp-goon-salvage">{{salvageLine}}</p>{{/if}}
    {{#each preview as |g|}}
    <div class="cp-goon-card" data-index="{{g.index}}">
      <div class="cp-goon-card-head">
        <span class="cp-goon-card-name">{{g.name}}</span>
        <span class="cp-goon-card-actions">
          <a class="cp-goon-icon" data-action="goonRerollOne" data-index="{{g.index}}"
             title="{{localize 'CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.RerollOne'}}"><i class="fas fa-dice"></i></a>
          <a class="cp-goon-icon" data-action="goonDeleteOne" data-index="{{g.index}}"
             title="{{localize 'CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.DeleteOne'}}"><i class="fas fa-trash"></i></a>
        </span>
      </div>
      {{!-- The rolled role, named per goon so the GM sees what each one BECAME before confirming.
            Rendered only for a Random batch — see _previewCard. --}}
      {{#if g.roleLine}}<p class="cp-goon-card-role">{{g.roleLine}}</p>{{/if}}
      <p class="cp-goon-card-stats">{{g.statLine}}</p>
      {{#if g.gearLine}}<p class="cp-goon-card-gear">{{g.gearLine}}</p>{{/if}}
      {{#if g.armorLine}}<p class="cp-goon-card-armor">{{g.armorLine}}</p>{{/if}}
      {{#if g.chromeLine}}<p class="cp-goon-card-chrome">{{g.chromeLine}}</p>{{/if}}
      {{#if g.honesty.length}}
      <ul class="cp-goon-honesty">
        {{#each g.honesty as |h|}}<li class="cp-goon-honesty-{{h.tone}}">{{h.text}}</li>{{/each}}
      </ul>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
    {{/each}}
  </div>
  {{/if}}

  {{!-- ── THE FUSED GENERATE BUTTON ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
  <div class="cp-goon-generate">
    <button type="button" class="cp-goon-btn cp-goon-go" data-action="{{generateAction}}">
      <i class="fas fa-users-gear"></i> {{generateLabel}}
    </button>
    <select id="cp-goon-dest" class="cp-goon-dest" title="{{localize 'CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.DestHint'}}">
      {{#each destinations as |d|}}
      <option value="{{d.value}}" {{#if d.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{d.label}}</option>
      {{/each}}
    </select>
    {{#if hasPreview}}
    <button type="button" class="cp-goon-btn" data-action="goonDiscard">
      <i class="fas fa-rotate-left"></i> {{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.Discard"}}
    </button>
    {{/if}}
  </div>

  {{#unless grade}}
  <p class="cp-goon-empty">{{localize "CYBERPUNK.GoonFactory.EmptyState"}}</p>
  {{/unless}}

  {{/if}}
</div>
